Recommends: camoufox | librewolf
Description: fingerprint-transparent web security testing workbench
 Camio is a local-first web security testing workbench built around the Camoufox
 anti-detect Firefox engine. Tool-originated traffic (Replay, Automate, Scanner,
 MCP) is sent through a BoringSSL-based impersonating client whose TLS/JA3/JA4 and
 HTTP/2 fingerprint is derived from, and pinned to, the same profile the managed
 browser uses, so authorized testing traffic does not stand out because of the
 tool.
 .
 It provides a CamioQL (HTTPQL-compatible) query language, a passive scanner,
 Intruder-class fuzzing, Convert/Decoder/Comparer, Burp/HAR importers, a
 sequencer, a native desktop app and an optional web UI, a plugin system, and a
 built-in MCP server — all under one shared scope and authorization policy.
 .
 Fingerprint transparency is a measured property, not a promise of
 undetectability. Camio is for authorized testing only.
